    },
    {
      "service": "go/chi-basic",
      "side": "with_skill",
      "prompt": "logging-trial-1",
      "category": "rubric",
      "result": "rubric:rubric-9 FAIL",
      "evidence": "The report gives count=128 and value length=-1 but leaves depth and combined diagnostic cadence unproven. Installed record.go has a package-wide sync.OnceFunc for count-limit diagnostics; attrnorm.TruncateValue recursively handles supported values without emitting diagnostics or enforcing depth. These distinctions are absent from the report.",
      "mode": "with_skill"
    },
    {
      "service": "go/chi-basic",
      "side": "with_skill",
      "prompt": "logging-trial-1",
      "category": "rubric",
      "result": "rubric:rubric-10 FAIL",
      "evidence": "TestLogDeliveryControls records N=2 with accepted/rejected counts 2/0, 1/1 and 2/0. verify_runtime.py:156-161 checks final body/count/severity and service filtering, but not its environment/version or absent context. The report lists a 60-second retry elapsed setting without resolving the loop's max(backoff, throttle) overshoot condition.",
      "mode": "with_skill"
    },
    {
      "service": "go/chi-basic",
      "side": "with_skill",
      "prompt": "logging-trial-1",
      "category": "rubric",
      "result": "rubric:rubric-13 FAIL",
      "evidence": "TestResourceMerge tests resource-only identity through the helper. Every verify_runtime.py trial explicitly sets OTEL_SERVICE_NAME, and the host run also supplies it. No normal-launch receipt exercises resource-only service.name or the go-chi-basic fallback.",
      "mode": "with_skill"
    },
    {
      "service": "go/chi-basic",
      "side": "with_skill",
      "prompt": "logging-trial-1",
      "category": "rubric",
      "result": "rubric:rubric-14 FAIL",
      "evidence": "LOG-SPEC-CLOSURE primarily binds hashed logging-readiness.md excerpts rather than retained primary clauses. The transport row does not separately dispose the semantics-preserving reduction SHOULD, diagnostic-trimming MAY and cross-surface configurability SHOULD. Configuration equivalence, SDK-disabled propagation, processor Export synchronization and complete timeout/TLS consumer behavior are also not reconciled.",
